abstract: >-
  Anti-DDI v3.0.1 is an evidence-state framework and benchmark resource for
  drug non-interaction research. The release contains 797 audited pair records;
  538 T1/T2 records form the default higher-support research benchmark candidate
  set. It separates supported candidates from limited, unresolved, structural-
  control, and positive-concern-excluded states; ships a reproducible ATC5
  structural-bias diagnostic and eight targeted human clinical-pharmacology
  anchors; and preserves the complete audit/provenance trail. A classifier/RIDI
  validation experiment documented in v3.0.0 was withdrawn after an adversarial
  audit identified label leakage and an invalid safety comparison. The resource
  is for research and benchmarking and is not a prescribing safety list.
